#: ../../source/guides/user/inputs.md:12
msgid "The formats repository"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/inputs.md:14
msgid ""
"A directory, tracked in its own version control, holding one recipe — a "
"**format** — per report layout. `analysis_finance_reports_formats` is one"
" such repository; there is nothing privileged about it, and you can "
"maintain your own."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/inputs.md:18
msgid "To start an empty one:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/inputs.md:24
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"That gives you a skeleton that supports no format yet. "
"{doc}`../formats/index` is how you add one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/inputs.md:26
msgid ""
"The repository is also what makes `--format` optional: it carries a "
"mapping from URL prefixes to format names, so a document downloaded from "
"a known address is read without being told which format it is. There is "
"no such inference for a local file — a path carries no evidence of who "
"published it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/inputs.md:30
msgid "The input database"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/inputs.md:32
msgid ""
"Which companies a run is looking for, organised into named **lists**. "
"`--target-list` names the lists to use, and a run with no list stops "
"before opening anything."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/inputs.md:35
msgid "For testing, a minimal database with a single list called `TEST`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/inputs.md:41
msgid ""
"It writes into `tests/input_db/` of the formats repository, deliberately:"
" a format's tests must fail because the *format* broke, never because "
"someone edited a company list maintained elsewhere. For real runs you "
"want a real database."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/inputs.md:45
msgid ""
"Two properties of the database change what a run finds, and both surprise"
" people:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/inputs.md:47
msgid ""
"**matching is first-match-wins, in file order.** The order of the file is"
" meaningful, not incidental. A run that seems to attribute a holding to "
"the wrong company is often reporting a database problem rather than an "
"extraction one;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/inputs.md:50
msgid ""
"a company absent from every named list is simply not looked for. Nothing "
"reports it, because nothing was asked about it."
msgstr ""

